# Ledger static site (Vercel)

Two surfaces under `dashboard/`:

| Path | Audience | Contents |
|------|----------|----------|
| `/` | Local / private cockpit | Sim equity curves (`invest sim`) |
| `/research` | **Public / portfolio** | Strategy selection cycle with **history** — no broker names or EUR amounts |

## Publish a research run

```powershell
invest research --publish-orbit
```

Writes:

- Private: `reports/research_cycle.html`, `proposal.html`, …
- Public: `dashboard/research/data/latest.json`
- Archive: `dashboard/research/data/history/<id>.json`
- Index: `dashboard/research/data/index.json` (history dropdown)
- Orbit copy: `public/ledger-research` in the Orbit checkout (`ORBIT_ROOT` or sibling `website` / `Orbit`)

Commit and push **Orbit `main`** (`public/ledger-research` only, no PR) so [alextouvras.com/ledger-research](https://alextouvras.com/ledger-research) updates. The Slack holdings automation is supposed to do that push.

Standing prompt: [`docs/HOLDINGS_AUTOMATION.md`](../docs/HOLDINGS_AUTOMATION.md).

## Deploy

```bash
npx vercel deploy dashboard --prod
```

Then link `https://<your-project>.vercel.app/research` from your website.

## Privacy rules (public page)

Shown: strategy KPIs, indexed equity chart, decision rationale, ticker actions with % weight deltas and momentum ranks.

Hidden: broker names (Nordnet / Saxo / OP), absolute € amounts, cash/book totals, capital sleeve map.
